# A position that is an int32 was extended by its sign for the test against the length, and that extension was the index of the address: movslq at every access.
# Against a length that fits 32 bits the word itself is compared, without a sign; behind the test it is not negative, and a word that a 32-bit operation made is extended by zeros already.
# byte: the length of a view of bytes may be 2 ** 32: there the test stays one of 64 bits.
# -- source: an-int32-position-costs-no-more-in-an-address-of-a-view-than-one-of-64-bits.ts
